{#
	One search result.

	Rendered by Zyppy\Search\Search\ResultRenderer for BOTH paths - the
	server-rendered first page and every live update fetched from
	/_zyppy/search/{moduleId} - so this file is the single place a result's
	markup is decided. That is what makes tl_module.searchTpl mean something:
	swap this template and both paths change together.

	Flat legacy identifier `search_zyppy`, no `.twig-root` marker anywhere above
	it - see search_zyppy_results.html.twig and mod_search_zyppy.html.twig for
	why. It matters most here: `searchTpl` is a dropdown built by
	Controller::getTemplateGroup('search_') (core tl_module.php:340), which
	throws for any identifier containing a slash, and existing tl_module rows
	already have the flat `search_zyppy` saved.

	--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	ESCAPED vs |raw - the pair that matters in a search result template.

	|raw:
	  context   ContextBuilder builds it as StringUtil::specialchars(...)
	            followed by a preg_replace that injects
	            `<mark class="highlight">$1</mark>` around every matched keyword
	            variant. So it is ALREADY escaped text with generated markup
	            layered on top. Escaping it again would show the reader
	            `&lt;mark class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;` instead of a highlight.

	Escaped - all of these are data:
	  link      the indexed page title. tl_search.title comes from
	            DomCrawler::text() (DefaultIndexer.php:47), i.e. DECODED plain
	            text, so a single escape here is exactly right.
	  href      NOTE: escaping is not the whole control for a URL. Twig does not
	            stop `javascript:` - htmlspecialchars() touches no character in
	            it - so the scheme check happens server side, in
	            SafeUrl::sanitise(), on the way into the DTO. A rejected URL
	            arrives here as '', which is why the link degrades to a <span>
	            below rather than rendering an empty href.
	  title     ResultEnricher passes StringUtil::stripInsertTags() only.
	  pageTeaser  tl_page.page_teaser is a plain textarea with
	              decodeEntities=>true and no rte/allowHtml (zyppy-page
	              tl_page.php:114-122). It is text, not editor HTML.
	  class, relevance, and every image attribute.

	IMAGES. `image` is built by contao.image.studio and carries src, srcset,
	sizes, width, height and alt - which is what finally makes tl_module.imgSize
	do something. `pageImage` is still set, to the same URL, so a site-specific
	search_* template written against the old bare-path shape keeps working.
	--------------------------------------------------------------------------
#}
<div class="{{ class|default('') }}">

	<h3>
		{%- if href|default('') -%}
			<a href="{{ href }}" title="{{ title|default('') }}">{{ link|default('') }}</a>
		{%- else -%}
			<span title="{{ title|default('') }}">{{ link|default('') }}</span>
		{%- endif %} <span class="relevance">[{{ relevance|default('') }}]</span>
	</h3>

	{% if image|default(null) and image.src|default('') %}
		<img src="{{ image.src }}" alt="{{ image.alt|default('') }}" class="page_image"
			{%- if image.srcset|default('') %} srcset="{{ image.srcset }}"{% endif %}
			{%- if image.sizes|default('') %} sizes="{{ image.sizes }}"{% endif %}
			{%- if image.width|default(null) %} width="{{ image.width }}"{% endif %}
			{%- if image.height|default(null) %} height="{{ image.height }}"{% endif %}>
	{% elseif pageImage|default('') %}
		<img src="{{ pageImage }}" alt="" class="page_image">
	{% endif %}

	{% if pageTeaser|default('') %}
		<p class="page_teaser">{{ pageTeaser }}</p>
	{% endif %}

	{% if hasContext|default(false) %}
		<p class="context">{{ context|default('')|raw }}</p>
	{% endif %}

</div>
